# Example 43: Diurnal microcosm - water column + anoxic sediment
# (doc/19 §5.4 B4 gate).  The sealed water patch has a phototroph that
# secretes acetate and an acetotroph feeding on it.  Sunlight follows a
# diurnal sine (light scalar, period 1440 ticks): during the day
# photosynthesis supersaturates O2 well above the 0.21 mM baseline, and
# at night the heterotroph's respiration sags O2 to ~0 while CO2 and
# acetate spike - the classic day/night oxygen flip.  The sediment patch
# is anoxic by construction (no O2 field) and receives settling biomass
# by dispersal; the whole microcosm conserves carbon (sealed).

#species name=producer photo=true photo_vmax=0.006 cn_ratio=8 maintenance=0.0005 secretion=acetate:0.0015
#species name=consumer substrate=acetate vmax=0.02 ks=0.1 cn_ratio=6 maintenance=0.002
#species name=sedimenter substrate=acetate vmax=0.015 ks=0.1 cn_ratio=6 maintenance=0.0015

#patch name=water kind=water carrying_capacity=1e6 initial.producer=500 initial.consumer=200 initial_nh4_mm=300 initial_no3_mm=100 substrate.co2.initial=2 substrate.acetate.initial=0 scalar.light.initial=500 scalar.light.kind=light scalar.light.forcing=diurnal dispersal.sediment=0.001
#patch name=sediment kind=chemostat anoxic=true initial.sedimenter=20 substrate.acetate.initial=0 initial_nh4_mm=300 dispersal.water=0.0005

#config backend=ecosystem

#sim kind=ecosystem ticks=2880 seed=7 fast_forward=false sample_every=288
#sim output=tick,water:producer,water:consumer,water:oxygen,water:co2,water:acetate,water:light,sediment:sedimenter
